# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VENDOR-DATA FENCE (see PROVENANCE.md). Everything below is built LOCALLY from
# YOUR licensed OpticStudio install by scripts/build_vendor_data.py and must
# NEVER be committed — committing it would redistribute license-derived data.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local SQLite builds (manual FTS5 corpus and any derived index)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# User-built data JSONs (derived from your install's .agf files / manual PDF /
# live-probe captures). The operand + tolerance catalogs embed verbatim-local
# manual descriptions, so they too are user-built + gitignored — only
# the synonyms/semantics SOURCES are committed.
packages/optivibe-reference/src/optivibe_reference/data/glass_catalog.json
packages/optivibe-reference/src/optivibe_reference/data/manual_manifest.json
packages/optivibe-reference/src/optivibe_reference/data/operand_catalog.json
packages/optivibe-reference/src/optivibe_reference/data/tolerance_operand_catalog.json
packages/optivibe-reference/src/optivibe_reference/data/operand_descriptions.json
packages/optivibe-reference/src/optivibe_reference/data/tolerance_operand_descriptions.json

# Verbatim manual-prose extracts (the paraphrase oracle) — never committed
packages/optivibe-reference/scripts/captures/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engine artifacts (regenerable OpticStudio companions / intermediates)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Engine binary companion (regenerable; the .zmx design itself is tracked)
*.ZDA

# Per-design intermediate candidate outputs (the BEST_* design is kept; candidates regenerate)
**/candidates/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Design-session leftovers — NEVER publish
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Running an optical design from inside this checkout drops artifacts here. They are
# fine locally and wrong in a public repository: `optivibe_interactions.jsonl` is a
# durable log of real tool calls, arguments and file paths, and a `.zmx` is a lens
# prescription — publishing one not deliberately chosen discloses design work by
# accident.
#
# This is safe-by-construction rather than safe-by-operator: the 0.1.4 publish staged
# its 22 payload paths explicitly BY NAME, so nothing leaked, but that came from the
# operator being careful on the day. Four permanent `??` entries also train the eye to
# skim the one `git status` section a publish decision depends on.
#
# Verified before adding: this repo tracks ZERO .png, .zmx or BEST_* files, so none of
# these rules can hide a real deliverable. NOTE the `**/candidates/` comment above says
# "the BEST_* design is kept" — that is a PRIVATE-repo convention that came across with
# the file. Here no design artifact is ever kept.
BEST_*.zmx
BEST_*.png
*_layout.png
optivibe_interactions.jsonl
optivibe_stdio.log
